  "id": "umami",
  "term": "umami",
  "definition": "Umami is one of the five basic taste qualities. In humans, it is mainly produced by free L-glutamic acid and is thought to help signal the presence of protein in food; its taste can also be strengthened by certain purine nucleotides such as IMP and GMP.",
